# The fields the checks read from documents that no tool decodes: a HelmRelease and the sources it
# names, as scripts/render reads them, and a FluxInstance, as scripts/pod-security-check reads it.
# Each reads them with jq, by exact name, and hands a tool only what it derives from them: helm a
# chart's URL, name and version as arguments and values files it writes, kustomize a kustomization
# it writes from a release's post-renderers or the instance's patches.
#
# roots: HelmRelease OCIRepository HelmRepository FluxInstance
#
# The API server drops a field of a custom resource that its schema does not name, by exact name,
# so the cluster ignores a key that only differs from one of these by case, as the checks would;
# the checks refuse such a key rather than skip it: one that encoding/json's folding matches to a
# field of the list (ASCII letters without regard to case, U+017F as s and U+212A as k). A type
# marked open holds other fields as well, which the checks do not read; every other type is all a
# tool is handed at that position, and any other key there is refused. One field a line, as in
# kustomization-fields; TYPE * open marks a type as open.
HelmRelease * open
HelmRelease apiVersion value
HelmRelease kind value
HelmRelease metadata Metadata
HelmRelease spec HelmReleaseSpec
Metadata * open
Metadata name value
Metadata namespace value
HelmReleaseSpec * open
HelmReleaseSpec chartRef ChartReference
HelmReleaseSpec chart Chart
HelmReleaseSpec valuesFrom []ValuesReference
HelmReleaseSpec values map
HelmReleaseSpec releaseName value
HelmReleaseSpec targetNamespace value
HelmReleaseSpec postRenderers []PostRenderer
HelmReleaseSpec test Test
ChartReference * open
ChartReference kind value
ChartReference name value
ChartReference namespace value
Chart * open
Chart spec ChartSpec
ChartSpec * open
ChartSpec chart value
ChartSpec version value
ChartSpec sourceRef SourceReference
ChartSpec valuesFiles value
